  "note": "Printed claims only (Step 6). Delta program: wires are programs.json wiresEffective, the 38-line basic sequence recognition circuit (VI-SEQREC) followed by the 36 Secret Code additions, 74 in all; as_printed is the same 74 in the same order, both lists read off BK6 printed p.51 (PDF p.57), image-checked at 150 and 300 dpi. This printing reads 6A/6J (the Combination Lock printing's 5A/6J conflict on PDF p.58 does not arise here). No wiring erratum: ER-40 (errata.pdf PDF p.4, 'The Secret Code (page 51): Note — to re-set the game, turn power off, then on again.') is procedure only, so errata_applied is empty and wires = as_printed; the script follows it by cycling power after the solved attempt (once solved, every relay is latched and no press can change the state). The p.52 procedure: wire the basic circuit, add the connections, set the slide switches (all six RIGHT = target 1000, the page's worked example), push pushbuttons 6 through 1. Asserted: light 1 on after 6-5-4-3-2-1; light 6 on after a wrong press (6, 5, 4, then 2 instead of 3); light 1 on after the next full 6-5-4-3-2-1 attempt, which is the printed 'automatically re-set for the next attempt'. The wrong press is a script choice; the page names no particular error. Each push is a press, a settle, a release and a settle; the page prints no hold time. Not asserted (derived, Step 7): light 1 off before the last push, light 6 off after the first correct push, relay and indicator-lamp states per press, the state after the ER-40 power cycle, and the solving order for any other switch setting. Light 6 is lit at power-on before any push (6H/6+ with 6A/6J on the normally-closed contact) and goes out when relay 6 latches on the first correct push; the page does not mention this. The code counts ('63 different codes', '720 different codes') and the starred-connection re-coding example (2T/2com, 6W/1com) are not observables and are not scripted.",
